      "writtenOn": "2024-07-03T21:17:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is also needed for STA and has been added to tearDownClientInterface() to account for that.\n\nMy primary use case is STA on/off (to populate WifiScanner cache) then AP on/off. \n\nThis error scenario is present regardless of AP and/or STA on/off. If we exclusively toggle 1 role (STA for example in the commit message) then we see the stale handlers accumulate.\n\nUnsubscribeRegDomainChange() is called in tearDownInterfaces, however, since the index is removed from the iface to index map within the role specific teardown method, the callback unregistration in the general teardown is skipped.",
      "parentUuid": "4706977f_7b2f442d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 175,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 175,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "d3b597d3173005bb4ac4e177140d825ca023fe5f",
