        "id": 3500282
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-03T21:17:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The callbacks are stored in a std::map, so the usual log(n) time complexity to locate the callback. Given there\u0027s only 1 wiphy_index at a time whenever the Wi-Fi driver is loaded, there will be a slight performance gain since we\u0027re removing entries.\n\nThis is only called on interface teardown when the interface exists, so not on the critcal path.",
